From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cappy Ishihara <cappy@cappuchino.xyz>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm: sun4i: a523: route DE scanout to TCON-LCD1

The TG5050 display pipeline uses mixer0 -> TCON-LCD1 (TCON index 1) ->
MIPI-DSI1. The initial A523 DE integration retained the HDMI bring-up
value tcon_id = 2, which selects the disabled TCON-TV0 output. Use the
actual LCD1 output selector instead.

The temporary current-line probe also used the TV0 register address. Point
it at the corresponding LCD1 current-line register so diagnostics describe
the active pipeline rather than the disabled HDMI path.

---
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun55i_de.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun55i_de.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun55i_de.c
@@ -340,1 +340,1 @@
-static unsigned int tcon_curline_phys = 0x55030fc;
+static unsigned int tcon_curline_phys = 0x55020fc;
@@ -523,2 +523,2 @@
-	/* HDMI is wired to tcon_tv0 = vendor tcon2 */
-	de->tcon_id = 2;
+	/* TG5050 routes mixer0 to TCON-LCD1, the vendor tcon1 output. */
+	de->tcon_id = 1;
